# Nested conditionals

Verifies an `if` body may contain further conditionals. The outer condition is
true, the directly nested condition is false, and the sibling nested condition
is true, so only the outer and sibling bodies print.

>>> source
const outer: int = 10
if (outer > 5) {
    print(1)
    if (outer > 15) {
        print(2)
    }
    if (outer > 8) {
        print(3)
    }
}

<<< stdout
1
3

<<< stderr
